@startuml seq-03-pay-always
!include style.iuml
title An agent pays a recipient set to Always\npayment: Idle → Queued → Signed → Sent → Included → Confirmed (C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C11, C12, C21)
autonumber "<b>0."

participant "Agent Mara\n(model)" as Agent
participant "wallet~__send\n(EffectTool, daemon)" as Tool
database "Store" as Store
participant "Wallet lane\n(durable task, FIFO)" as Lane
participant "Signer\nsupervisor + child" as Signer
participant "OS keychain" as KC
participant "RPC / Base" as Chain
participant "Receipt follower" as Follower
participant "Chat\n(card)" as Chat

Agent -> Tool : wallet~__send {to: "0x12ab…9f04", amount: "5", token: "USDC"}
Tool -> Tool : expand: parse "5" in USDC's 6 decimals,\ncanonicalize to EIP-55 on the wallet's network (C3 steps 4, 5)
Tool -> Store : admission commit (effectRun, withinPermission)
note right of Store
  One commit, C3 order: wallet ready; Mara on for it; tool on (allowedAs);
  arguments; identity; wallet can sign now; rule: no Deny(wallet, Ana),
  Always(Mara, wallet, 0x12ab…) covers it, amount not bound;
  available = balance at block b − reservations − fee reserve ≥ 5 (C11).
  row: Idle · call [wallet_usable and payer == 'agent' and eff == 'always' and fits] → Queued
end note
Store --> Tool : payment I queued in lane L (id from the tool task id, C14), reservation 5 USDC + fees
Tool -> Chat : card "Paying Ana 5 USDC" (a card shows even when nobody was asked)
Tool --> Agent : queued; outcome follows in the chat

Lane -> Store : read the head of the FIFO: I
Lane -> Chain : latest block, base fee, priority fee, L1 fee upper bound
Lane -> Signer : signTransfer(I, nonce = ledger.next, chainId 84532), request id
Signer -> KC : get "<home-id>/wallet/<address>"
KC --> Signer : secret
Signer -> Signer : derive == record's address (C16);\nEIP-1559 transfer(address,uint256), extraEntropy false
Signer --> Lane : raw bytes (the key stays in the child)
Lane -> Store : fused start commit (the burn point, C4)
note right of Store
  Re-checks: I still Queued, not refused by a cancel or a Deny sweep;
  C3 steps 1, 2, 6, 7, 8 against the rules as they are now;
  ledger unchanged since signing (compare-and-set, F-3).
  Takes nonce n = ledger.next, appends version {raw, keccak256(raw)},
  I → Signed. Synced per commit before any broadcast (C21).
  row: Queued · start_commit [not ledger_moved and start_ok and fits] → Signed
end note
Lane -> Chain : eth_sendRawTransaction(stored raw)
Chain --> Lane : hash (or "already known": the same bytes are harmless)
Lane -> Store : I → Sent
note right of Store : row: Signed · broadcast → Sent

loop poll 2 s while awaited (a logs subscription where offered)
  Follower -> Chain : eth_getTransactionReceipt(hash of each version)
  Chain --> Follower : null
end
Chain --> Follower : receipt, status 1, at latest
Follower -> Store : I → Included; the nonce lease is released (one in flight, C5)
note right of Store : row: Sent · receipt [blk == 'own'] → Included
Follower -> Store : shown as "Included (safe)" once the block is at safe (about 2 min on Base; a display, R-4)
Follower -> Chain : is that block finalized? (about 20 min on Base)
Chain --> Follower : yes
Follower -> Store : I → Confirmed; reservation released
note right of Store : row: Included · finality [blk_fin and blk_ok] → Confirmed (Settle)
Follower -> Chat : "Paid Ana 5 USDC · Confirmed" (balance after)
Chat --> Agent : the outcome, as data

note over Agent, Chat
  Always pays its recipient whatever amount, up to what is in the wallet: the balance is the cap (requirement 2).
  A status-0 receipt, proven from two sources (C7), gives Failed at finalized (Included · finality [blk_fin and not blk_ok] → Failed); a reorg gives
  Included · reorg → Sent and the stored bytes are rebroadcast (C12). The absence of a receipt never ends a payment.
end note
@enduml
